dialect protocol
protocol stdio.obj.snapshot
version 1
schema stdio.obj
start body

# P2-FG1: `stdio.obj` is TEXT-NATIVE (per `📖️phase2-design.md`'s own classification table — plain
# Wavefront OBJ keyword-line text, no binary structure of its own) — there is no "binary OBJ"; the
# pack container IS the SEMIO envelope wrapping this artifact's own real OBJ text bytes verbatim
# (`ArtifactPack::encode_pack_with`, `../../🦀️component.rs`:217-227: `engine::encode_obj(self)
# .into_bytes()` passed straight to `store::semio_format::wrap_binary` — no `pack_rt::
# encode_document` structured record, since an OBJ document has no `RecordSpec`-shaped binary
# layout to walk against, same reason the sibling json/csv/txt text-native pilots are modeled this
# way, confirmed by direct reading, not assumed).
#
# The framework-level SEMIO envelope itself (magic `0x8953454D0D0A1A0A` + LE u32 token length +
# UTF-8 token) is described ONCE, at
# `🧰️framework/🛍️products/💻️os/🔨️modules/🧬️semio/📡️protocol/📡️component.protocol.semio`
# (P2-M3 deliverable 3) — this file does NOT re-describe that framing. Per that file's own report
# (`p2-m3-report.md` §5 point 4) and confirmed against the real harness this file is validated by
# (`m5_handcrafted_protocol_conformance`'s `inner_payload_from_semio_example`, which `unwrap_binary`s
# the `.pack.semio` fixture before handing bytes to `walk_protocol`): this file models the bytes as
# if the walk already starts AT the payload, past the envelope. Cross-artifact `use semio.envelope`
# is not yet functional at walk time (confirmed unchanged through every prior pilot wave), so the
# envelope is deliberately NOT re-inlined here either — the payload-only framing below is both the
# honest current mechanism boundary and the literal shape the real test exercises.
#
# The payload itself is opaque, unstructured UTF-8 bytes at the BINARY-protocol layer by
# construction — its real internal grammar (the keyword-statement structure above) is
# `📝️text/📖️component.grammar.semio`'s job, not this protocol dialect's; free-form OBJ text has no
# fixed byte width to declare here — `chain ... utf8` is the honest boundary, the same treatment
# json/csv/txt's own text-native protocol files give an opaque text payload segment.
framing record
chain payload utf8
